WEBVTT

01:27.140 --> 01:29.980
<b>AQUARION</b>

01:32.310 --> 01:34.320
The seven wonders of Eno Academy?

01:34.320 --> 01:38.680
Yeah. Like sometimes the boys and 
girls bathrooms switch places.

01:39.810 --> 01:40.740
The heck is that about?

01:40.940 --> 01:45.490
And the giant mirror that pulls you 
in if you stare into it at 4:44 p.m.,

01:45.850 --> 01:47.370
the smiling anatomical model,

01:47.370 --> 01:50.180
the <i>Mona Lisa</i> that looks away 
when you make eye contact,

01:50.180 --> 01:51.210
also...

01:51.720 --> 01:52.900
What was it?

01:53.580 --> 01:56.710
Oh, right. 
The running Ninomiya Kinjiro statue.

01:57.080 --> 02:00.760
On top of that, when the gymnasium is empty,

02:00.760 --> 02:04.460
you can hear a "bounce, bounce" 
like someone is dribbling a ball.

02:05.800 --> 02:08.380
And that's scary? I wouldn't know.

02:08.380 --> 02:10.970
Yeah. But that's you, Sakko.

02:11.830 --> 02:14.760
That's only six. What's the last one?

02:15.090 --> 02:16.400
That one is...

02:17.340 --> 02:19.350
The ghost in the library.

02:19.350 --> 02:22.330
It calls to you from 
behind a bookcase and says,

02:22.330 --> 02:23.440
"Can we be friends?"

02:22.610 --> 02:23.440
Huh?

02:23.440 --> 02:25.240
No way. It's Kokkuri-san.

02:25.240 --> 02:28.910
Huh? What about the ghost that comes 
back for revenge against bullies?

02:28.910 --> 02:29.520
Hm?

02:29.520 --> 02:32.900
No, no. It's the one about the 
mysterious transfer student.

02:34.230 --> 02:37.220
When a student dies, a month later or so

02:37.220 --> 02:41.200
a transfer student who
 looks exactly the same shows up!

02:42.700 --> 02:44.270
For the last wonder,

02:44.270 --> 02:47.910
everyone had heard different things, 
and nobody knew which one was right.

02:47.910 --> 02:49.220
Ever hear those, Sakko?

02:49.220 --> 02:51.270
No, I never had any friends anyway.

02:51.270 --> 02:54.680
My bro told me that when 
you're in the entrance hall

02:54.680 --> 02:58.570
and nobody is around, 
sometimes you can hear a piano go "plink"!

02:58.570 --> 03:00.280
Huh?

03:09.220 --> 03:10.820
What's wrong, Momo?

03:10.820 --> 03:14.190
Huh? Did you just hear a piano note?

03:14.190 --> 03:17.790
What are you talking about? 
Come on, P.E.'s next. Let's go!

03:17.790 --> 03:18.980
Uh, okay.

03:22.370 --> 03:25.460
What's the matter now?

03:25.460 --> 03:30.070
It feels like someone's 
been following me all day.

03:31.450 --> 03:32.950
Hey, you hear?

03:32.950 --> 03:33.920
About what?

03:33.920 --> 03:36.480
The transfer student. 
They say he's really cute!

03:36.480 --> 03:38.650
What? No. It's a girl, right? In first-year.

03:38.650 --> 03:41.430
No! It's a boy in third-year.

03:41.430 --> 03:42.360
Huh?

03:42.580 --> 03:46.150
Speaking of ghosts, do you think 
those things are ghost, too?

03:46.150 --> 03:46.990
What things?

03:46.990 --> 03:49.480
The ones we see when Aquarion unites.

03:49.990 --> 03:53.370
Ichiki-san said that they're our past lives.

03:53.370 --> 03:55.370
Oh. Yeah, that sounds right.

03:55.660 --> 03:58.890
In a past life, 
Momohime-senpai and I were sisters.

03:58.890 --> 04:01.370
Huh? How did you learn that?

04:01.370 --> 04:05.220
During our date at the aquarium, 
we both had the same vision.

04:05.220 --> 04:08.220
Just the two of us... in another world.

04:09.050 --> 04:13.540
Past lives, huh? Yeah, she was always 
daydreaming about stuff like that.

04:19.760 --> 04:21.780
Sorry. You guys go ahead.

04:21.780 --> 04:22.380
Uh...

04:22.380 --> 04:23.140
Huh?

04:23.140 --> 04:25.360
Hey, wasn't this the boys bathroom?

04:26.560 --> 04:27.490
Pardon me.

04:28.980 --> 04:29.910
Oh.

04:32.500 --> 04:33.430
Uh...

04:34.750 --> 04:35.890
Huh?

04:40.420 --> 04:41.630
Oh!

04:41.630 --> 04:42.900
What's wrong?

04:43.880 --> 04:46.250
I... just saw Sayo.

04:46.540 --> 04:47.670
Huh?

04:49.910 --> 04:51.890
<i>Did Ichiki's ghost really appear?</i>

04:51.890 --> 04:55.510
<i>I heard her ghost appeared in the library.</i>

04:55.510 --> 04:58.720
<i>So that really was Sayo! I saw her, too.</i>

04:58.720 --> 04:59.920
<i>Scary!</i>

04:59.920 --> 05:02.820
<i>You sure it wasn't the the bullied 
kid who committed suicide</i>

05:02.820 --> 05:04.650
<i>and came back for revenge?</i>

05:04.650 --> 05:06.220
<i>That seven wonders thing?</i>

05:06.220 --> 05:08.560
<i>It's cause you guys always 
left Ichiki out, right?</i>

05:08.560 --> 05:09.940
<i>We didn't leave her out,</i>

05:09.940 --> 05:11.680
<i>and she didn't even commit suicide.</i>

05:11.680 --> 05:13.250
<i>So shut up, dummy!</i>

05:14.360 --> 05:19.000
Most likely, that is a leftover from 
before this universe split into two.

05:19.000 --> 05:23.130
It's a remnant of consciousness from the 
super-civilization period that existed then.

05:23.130 --> 05:25.030
Super-civilization period?

05:25.030 --> 05:25.960
Yes.

05:26.650 --> 05:30.700
Research shows that talented 
Element cadets like Ichiki Sayo

05:30.700 --> 05:33.770
often carry memories of their past lives.

05:34.850 --> 05:38.560
And as you all have the ability to 
turn your emotions into energy,

05:38.560 --> 05:42.290
it is also likely that you are responsive 
to the traces of spiritual energy

05:42.290 --> 05:44.140
that super-civilization 
has left throughout time.

05:44.140 --> 05:45.820
Um...

05:46.290 --> 05:49.840
You see, the idea of past lives 
really isn't that unscientific.

05:50.290 --> 05:54.680
It just means that you can sometimes 
see things that normal people can't.

05:56.000 --> 06:00.710
Saruta-sensei, I heard a new transfer 
student was coming late in the term.

06:00.710 --> 06:02.880
Would that student be...

06:02.880 --> 06:05.600
As I'm sure you've guessed, 
the new student is an Element cadet.

06:05.600 --> 06:07.680
And a very promising one at that.

06:07.970 --> 06:09.660
Oh, really?

06:10.310 --> 06:14.360
Sakko, think the Ichiki-san you saw 
was actually that transfer student?

06:14.360 --> 06:15.120
What?

06:15.120 --> 06:18.520
Uh, actually, Sakko said he saw Ichiki-san.

06:18.520 --> 06:22.070
Other students saw her, too. 
I got some chat messages about it.

06:22.070 --> 06:27.140
Could that mean the universe's ability 
to self-correct is still in effect?

06:27.580 --> 06:30.150
Unfortunately, that is not 
what's happening here.

06:30.570 --> 06:36.160
We all witnessed her death and cried over 
her remains at the funeral, didn't we?

06:37.100 --> 06:42.910
At this point in time, each one of us is
 living in a universe where she has died.

06:43.840 --> 06:49.390
Her death is now a confirmed fact, 
whichever universe you are in.

06:55.020 --> 06:59.070
Then the thing Sakko saw 
was a r-real ghost?!

06:59.070 --> 07:00.100
Ah, that may have been—

07:00.490 --> 07:01.600
Oh!

07:04.110 --> 07:05.040
Sayo?

07:05.740 --> 07:07.160
Wait, Sayo!

07:16.790 --> 07:17.720
Huh...

07:19.420 --> 07:21.450
So she is real.

07:21.450 --> 07:22.880
Where did she go?

07:22.880 --> 07:23.940
There she is!

07:27.660 --> 07:29.040
You guys go that way.

07:29.040 --> 07:29.730
Yeah.

07:29.040 --> 07:29.970
Okay.

07:35.440 --> 07:36.760
O-Over there!

08:00.770 --> 08:01.800
Hey.

08:03.960 --> 08:04.900
Who are you?

08:06.130 --> 08:10.820
The song that the stars play is the 
melody that tunes the universe.

08:23.340 --> 08:24.810
A Mythic Beast!

08:24.810 --> 08:25.740
What timing.

08:25.740 --> 08:27.000
Can't be helped. Let's go.

08:27.000 --> 08:27.930
Yeah.

08:32.170 --> 08:33.560
Huh?

08:43.260 --> 08:47.310
<i>For your safety, access to surrounding 
areas is now prohibited.</i>

08:47.310 --> 08:51.000
<i>All citizens, please seek 
shelter immediately.</i>

08:51.800 --> 08:54.920
<i>Yacht harbor, launch sequence 
initiated. Prepare for launch.</i>

08:54.920 --> 08:58.730
<i>Iwaya cave, open bay doors.</i>

08:58.730 --> 09:00.680
<i>Catapult launch path all green.</i>

09:02.440 --> 09:04.750
<i>Vector Siegel, launch!</i>

09:07.390 --> 09:09.820
<i>Vector Feoh, launch!</i>

09:13.030 --> 09:15.440
<i>Vector Tir, launch!</i>

09:18.220 --> 09:19.650
Another drill?

09:19.650 --> 09:21.530
There have been a lot recently.

09:21.530 --> 09:23.970
Those are the Space Preservation 
Agency's Machines.

09:23.970 --> 09:24.970
They are?

09:31.050 --> 09:34.550
The Mythic Beast is already 
halfway through the rift!

09:39.420 --> 09:40.650
At Lake Ashi?

09:42.550 --> 09:45.920
The members DEAVA chose are Otori Sakko-kun,

09:45.920 --> 09:48.950
Amaha Momohime-kun, and Hatano Toshi-kun.

09:49.230 --> 09:50.350
Roger.

09:50.950 --> 09:52.030
Hurry!

09:52.300 --> 09:54.310
You don't have to tell me.

09:57.830 --> 10:00.740
It's our first time together, 
Toshi-kun. Good luck!

10:00.740 --> 10:01.750
Thanks!

10:07.160 --> 10:08.740
What is that thing?

10:09.420 --> 10:10.930
It's coming this way!

10:25.470 --> 10:27.680
Hurry up and unite!

10:28.010 --> 10:29.100
Let's do it!

10:29.630 --> 10:33.270
Stop! Your mana gauges haven't 
reached union levels yet!

10:42.660 --> 10:44.290
What the hell is wrong?

10:48.250 --> 10:51.630
No! The town is that way! 
There are too many people!

10:52.170 --> 10:56.490
<i>Amaha-san, Otori-kun, get rid 
of any intrusive thoughts!</i>

10:57.850 --> 10:59.790
Pull yourself together, Sakko!

10:57.850 --> 10:59.790
Pull it together, Momohime!

11:00.310 --> 11:04.330
It's fine. It's better if you 
don't rush and unite as Siegel.

11:04.330 --> 11:08.220
DEAVA wants you to unite with 
Tir as the head this time.

11:09.020 --> 11:10.470
Huh? Me?

11:10.470 --> 11:12.330
Pull it together, Toshi!

11:10.470 --> 11:12.330
Pull yourself together, Toshi-kun!

11:12.700 --> 11:15.120
But I'm not ready!

11:15.640 --> 11:19.410
Good! The mana gauges have 
finally reached union levels!

11:22.590 --> 11:25.280
Then let's go, Sakko, Momohime-senpai!

11:25.280 --> 11:25.870
Yes!

11:25.280 --> 11:26.210
Yeah!

11:28.650 --> 11:31.580
Mythic Star Union! Go, Aquarion!

11:43.520 --> 11:44.450
Toshi!

11:55.520 --> 11:57.810
<i>Aquarion Tir!</i>

12:32.820 --> 12:37.180
Tir's specialty is using edged 
weapons in close combat.

12:41.640 --> 12:45.290
Siegel wouldn't be able to get close 
enough for hand-to-hand combat,

12:45.290 --> 12:48.040
and Feoh's arrows would probably 
just bounce right off it.

12:48.040 --> 12:51.990
However, Tir's edged weapon can engage it!

13:07.130 --> 13:09.560
Atone for your sins!

13:10.750 --> 13:13.250
As I raise this sword,

13:13.250 --> 13:17.750
I pray not for the eternal 
salvation of the wicked!

13:18.180 --> 13:22.440
Executioner's Sword of Judgment!

13:22.400 --> 13:24.700
<b>Infinite Conviction Sword</b>

13:41.520 --> 13:42.400
<i>Did we get it?</i>

13:42.400 --> 13:43.570
<i>It didn't cut through!</i>

14:01.480 --> 14:02.810
It got away.

14:02.810 --> 14:05.160
Place a 500-meter radius 
blockade around the stake!

14:05.160 --> 14:07.720
Expedite the evacuation of 
residents and tourists!

14:11.190 --> 14:14.620
<i>They've finally driven a 
nail into our coffin.</i>

14:14.620 --> 14:16.960
Yes. I apologize.

14:16.960 --> 14:18.920
It's okay! It's just one.

14:18.920 --> 14:23.200
They didn't form a triangle yet, 
so it doesn't change the big picture.

14:23.510 --> 14:26.070
<i>However, the situation is rapidly changing.</i>

14:26.070 --> 14:29.510
<i>We need to move our plans along. Quickly.</i>

14:29.510 --> 14:34.090
<i>That's why we sent our trump card to 
the school as a transfer student.</i>

14:34.470 --> 14:39.250
Ahh. I'm surprised that they decided 
to release the child to us.

14:39.250 --> 14:42.560
I know what this will mean to them.

14:42.560 --> 14:45.310
<i>That was an arrangement between us 
and them. You need not understand.</i>

14:45.940 --> 14:50.530
<i>If this succeeds, you will no longer 
struggle to find replacement Elements.</i>

14:51.070 --> 14:53.650
Do you think it will all go well?

14:53.650 --> 14:57.230
You've gotta make sure it 
does, Munakata-sensei.

14:57.550 --> 15:00.800
Speaking of which, the item 
we discussed is now ready.

15:00.800 --> 15:03.780
It's based on Aquarion Siegel.

15:03.780 --> 15:07.550
It uses an artificial Mythic Stone 
as its mana amplification device.

15:08.090 --> 15:10.560
<i>The HAKOBUNE will soon be complete.</i>

15:10.560 --> 15:13.250
<i>After that, we just have to
wait for Enoshima Academy to</i>

15:13.250 --> 15:15.170
<i>produce a morphogenetic field.</i>

15:29.120 --> 15:31.110
Oh, thou with defiled wings.

15:31.110 --> 15:32.550
Make thy case.

15:33.120 --> 15:35.850
Th-These wings are all her fault!

15:35.850 --> 15:39.710
If you pull out her wings, 
my wings will go back to normal!

15:40.740 --> 15:42.020
Why, you...

15:42.780 --> 15:44.810
Mulua Satene, our Goddess!

15:44.810 --> 15:45.750
Pass your judgment!

15:51.190 --> 15:53.230
Judgment has been passed.

15:53.230 --> 15:57.290
Tear out their wings and banish 
them from the land of Naacal.

15:58.310 --> 15:59.760
You can't!

16:05.730 --> 16:09.030
What are you laughing about? 
This is all your fault!

16:09.500 --> 16:10.660
It's your—

16:11.400 --> 16:15.820
Let me go. Let me go! Let go!

16:22.970 --> 16:27.410
Do you think that stuff is 
from our past life after all?

16:27.410 --> 16:32.420
For the remnants of some spiritual 
civilization, it sure is hard-core.

16:33.790 --> 16:37.080
I guess a bunch of people died 
in that last battle, huh?

16:38.170 --> 16:39.100
Hm?

16:43.310 --> 16:58.070
<b>Satela</b>

16:43.310 --> 16:58.070
<b>Hakone</b>

16:43.310 --> 16:58.070
<b>Mount Hakone  Evacuation Orders  Fear of Possible Secondary Disasters</b>

16:43.310 --> 16:58.070
<b>Owakudani, Hakone
About 1:00 p.m.</b>

16:43.310 --> 16:58.070
Over 50 Dead in Landslide

16:43.740 --> 16:46.900
<i>It is believed that over fifty people 
were buried in the landslide</i>

16:46.900 --> 16:49.500
<i>that accompanied the eruption in Owakudani.</i>

16:49.930 --> 16:52.710
<i>Desperate rescue efforts continue even now</i>

16:52.710 --> 16:55.210
<i>and an evacuation advisory was 
announced for nearby areas</i>

16:55.210 --> 16:57.500
<i>as the threat of secondary 
disasters still lingers.</i>

16:58.390 --> 17:02.320
Even though the universe 
corrected the truth about it.

17:02.320 --> 17:05.470
A lot of people were still saved 
thanks to you, Toshi-kun.

17:06.200 --> 17:08.350
Momohime-senpai...

17:08.350 --> 17:14.130
Anyway, we've got to do what we can, 
or else there will be even more victims.

17:14.130 --> 17:16.560
Guys, let's give it our best shot!

17:16.560 --> 17:17.670
Yeah!

17:17.990 --> 17:20.290
This pep talk stuff is so...

17:37.600 --> 17:38.830
Sayo?

17:42.680 --> 17:43.860
Sayo!

17:44.200 --> 17:45.130
Hm?

17:47.650 --> 17:48.580
Wait.

17:49.070 --> 17:51.590
Aren't you Ichiki-san?

17:51.870 --> 17:53.840
Who the hell are you?

17:55.270 --> 17:59.000
How's it goin'? I'm Ichiki Hana 
from first-year class three.

17:59.000 --> 18:00.570
Ichiki, you mean...

18:01.660 --> 18:04.290
I'm really supposed to start tomorrow.

18:04.290 --> 18:05.960
Today I'm just takin' a look around.

18:05.960 --> 18:08.310
Are you actually the transfer student?

18:08.680 --> 18:13.480
Are y'all actually my big sister's friends?

18:14.050 --> 18:15.210
Big sister?

18:16.230 --> 18:19.770
Ichiki Sayo's my big sis!

18:19.770 --> 18:20.930
Huh?

18:22.450 --> 18:24.530
Sayo had a sister?

18:30.310 --> 18:34.470
Hey, Momo-nee, did you know 
she had a little sister?

18:34.920 --> 18:38.580
I did hear her say she 
loved her little sister.

18:39.080 --> 18:43.300
She was sad that she couldn't see her 
because it would put her at risk.

18:44.640 --> 18:47.000
Does she have an incurable 
disease or something?

18:47.000 --> 18:50.070
Maybe that's why she wasn't at the funeral.

18:50.070 --> 18:52.260
Wait. But she seems totally fine.

18:54.660 --> 18:59.720
From what I saw, my big sis was good 
at studyin', was real nice to people,

18:59.720 --> 19:04.130
and could do anything, 
'cause she was super perfect!

19:05.480 --> 19:07.600
Yeah, she was.

19:07.600 --> 19:08.910
Was she?

19:09.280 --> 19:14.830
She wrote about you guys, Momohime-senpai 
and Sakko-senpai, in her letters to me.

19:14.830 --> 19:16.420
She wrote letters?

19:16.420 --> 19:17.450
Yup.

19:17.450 --> 19:20.810
Said she was sick of watchin' you 
do risky stuff, Sakko-senpai.

19:25.170 --> 19:30.360
On the other hand, she said Momohime-senpai 
was super smart, good at sports,

19:30.360 --> 19:31.690
and real nice!

19:32.200 --> 19:35.700
But, see, I didn't believe 
any of that until today.

19:35.700 --> 19:39.030
I thought there's like no way 
anybody's more perfect than my sis.

19:39.030 --> 19:41.340
I don't think I'm perfect at all, though.

19:41.340 --> 19:43.310
But I watched ya all day.

19:43.310 --> 19:44.350
You watched us?

19:45.760 --> 19:48.150
Oh. So that was you the whole time?

19:48.150 --> 19:50.150
Folks say I look just like my sis.

19:50.150 --> 19:51.560
Does she?

19:51.560 --> 19:52.490
No way.

19:53.670 --> 19:54.810
Hana-chan!

20:02.980 --> 20:05.000
The dead second-year girl's little sister?

20:05.000 --> 20:06.830
Why did she change her looks?

20:06.830 --> 20:09.320
Didn't want to scare people 
looking just like her sister.

20:09.320 --> 20:11.000
So she's gonna be class clown now?

20:13.050 --> 20:13.980
Ew...

20:17.180 --> 20:19.420
Ta-da! How does that look?

20:26.710 --> 20:28.090
Who's that?

20:28.530 --> 20:30.580
The new transfer student is really cool!

20:30.580 --> 20:31.470
Let's go see!

20:31.470 --> 20:32.400
Yeah.

20:33.410 --> 20:35.140
Good morning, Momo.

20:35.140 --> 20:36.320
Good morning.

20:36.320 --> 20:39.590
Hey, you hear about the 
mystery transfer student yet?

20:39.590 --> 20:43.080
Mystery? We met yesterday.

20:43.080 --> 20:46.180
There's no mystery. Only cuteness!

20:46.180 --> 20:48.000
Huh? Seriously?

20:48.000 --> 20:50.210
Maybe she's finally 
taking an interest in boys.

20:50.210 --> 20:52.340
Huh? What are you talking about?

20:55.380 --> 20:57.260
Where did you move from?

20:57.260 --> 20:58.370
Got any hobbies?

20:58.860 --> 21:00.450
What's your favorite food?

21:01.580 --> 21:03.140
What did you eat for breakfast?

21:04.570 --> 21:06.780
Oh, so that's the transfer student.

21:10.530 --> 21:13.740
Wasn't Hana-chan supposed 
to be the transfer student?

21:13.740 --> 21:15.700
I guess it was that guy.

21:25.550 --> 21:30.500
I promised we would be one, didn't I? 
Let me keep that promise.

21:31.610 --> 21:32.540
All right.

21:33.390 --> 21:35.360
Huh?!

21:41.480 --> 21:45.180
What's Momohime-senpai thinking anyway?

21:46.190 --> 21:48.780
I thought she couldn't experience love.

21:53.780 --> 21:56.420
Momohime-senpai!

22:02.240 --> 22:03.750
I, like,

22:04.190 --> 22:05.840
decided, Momohime-senpai,

22:06.880 --> 22:09.180
to kill you, 'kay?
